# Angular Template Simplicity

Templates are for layout and binding names — not data shaping.

## Rules

- Do **not** call injected services or unwrap signals in HTML (`service.items()`, `stats()?.field`, `??` defaults)
- Do **not** chain optional access, nullish coalescing, or slice/filter in templates
- Expose view-ready values from the component class as **getters**, **computed signals**, or small methods used for actions/formatting
- Inject services as **`private readonly`** when the template only uses getters
- Pipes in templates are fine when bound to a simple property (`copayRate | pct`)

## Examples

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
[val]="(finance.stats()?.copayRate ?? 0) | pct"
@for (item of charge.items(); track item.id)

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
[val]="copayRate | pct"
@for (item of items; track item.id)
```

```typescript
// Component class
private readonly finance = inject(FinanceService);

public get copayRate(): number
{
    return this.finance.stats()?.copayRate ?? 0;
}

public get items(): ChargeItem[]
{
    return this.charge.items();
}
```
